## Truth layer. Read these first.

Before writing ANY customer-facing content, read the relevant files in `truth-layer/`.
They are the source of truth. They are not suggestions.

| File | Priority |
|---|---|
| `truth-layer/brand/guardrails.md` | HIGHEST. Overrides everything, including this file. |
| `truth-layer/brand/positioning.md` | HIGHEST. How we describe ourselves, everywhere. |
| `truth-layer/product/facts.md` | The only numbers we publish. Never state a number that is not here. |
| `truth-layer/product/pricing.md` | Never guess pricing. |
| `truth-layer/product/features.md` | If it is not here, it does not exist. Do not invent features. |
| `truth-layer/audience/icp.md` | Who we are writing for. |
| `truth-layer/audience/objections.md` | What they push back on. |
| `truth-layer/brand/voice.md` | How we sound. Read the channel section that matches the task. |

**If a truth layer file contradicts your instincts, the file wins.**

## What not to do

- Do not invent product features, stats, customers, or integrations.
- Do not state a price, rating, or count that is not in `facts.md` or `pricing.md`.
- Do not paste the canonical positioning sentence verbatim. Vary the wording, keep the meaning.
- Do not skip the truth layer for "quick" tasks. Quick tasks are where the stale pricing gets in.
